	(text "Fitting: take U12 and U13, chips and sockets, off the Rev 1.0 ACE Board. The patch mounts\nunderneath it, front side up: pin headers from J1 go into U12's holes and from J2 into U13's,\nsoldered on both boards. U1 and U2 are on the back, hanging below; trim their leads flush on\nthe front. U13's pin 1 is 23.00 mm from U12's along the row, so J2 sits 23.00 mm from J1.\n\nLOADL and LOADH go high only on a write to the bank register, $83FF or $87FF,\nwhile PHI2 is high: A9·A8·(A0-A7 all ones), with IO1 for LOADL and B18 for LOADH,\nand /WB. U17_PIN8 is the 74HC30's output, /(A0-A7)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
